.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt SSH3-CERT 1
.Os ssh3-c
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3-cert
.Nd the PKI utility of the ssh3-c set
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
carries the one-shot operations of the certificate life outside the
always-running daemon
(.Xr ssh3-server 8 ) :
the OpenWrt flash and the resident memory of the daemon stay clean
of the PKI waves (the client certificates, the
ssh3-ca).
The daemon consumes the ready files this utility prepares; the
rotation rides the reopen channel.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm trust-update Op Fl -trust-update-url Ar url
Fetch the trust bundle, validate it (every PEM block a
certificate, the count floor) and land it atomically as
.Pa ~/.ssh3/trust-bundle.pem
- the manifest next to it names the source and the SHA-256; the
previous copy stays on any failure (the offline scheduler run is
the plain shape).
Exit 0 lands a fresh bundle, 255 keeps the stale one.
The default source is
.Li https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem
(the Mozilla set of the curl distribution); the scheduler units
.Pa ssh3-trust-update.{service,timer}
call this once a day.
.It Cm ticket-key Ar file
Generate a session ticket key file (the nginx 80-byte form: 16
name + 32 hmac + 32 aes, 0600) the daemon reads at the start -
the pre-seeded key survives the first daemon lifetime (the
.Xr ssh3-server 8
.Fl -session-ticket-key-file
twin of the wave 13).
.It Cm keygen | Cm selfsign | Cm csr | Cm sign
The phase 3/4 commands (the client certificates, the ssh3-ca):
the stubs refuse with the phase note for now.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/trust-bundle.pem , Pa ~/.ssh3/trust-bundle.pem.man
The landed bundle and its manifest.
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/aia-cache/
The fetched intermediate cache of the client chase.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3 1 ,
.Xr ssh3-server 8
